{"step_index":522,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-05-20T18:11:22Z","content":"I have found the root cause of the issue and implemented a fix. \n\n### Why this happened:\nThe \"Assigned Clients\" UI components across the media roles (Photographer, Videographer, Drone) had a hardcoded filter (`!isAccepted`) that explicitly removed any assignments where `accepted: false`. This was preventing new, unaccepted leads from rendering on the screen, even though the Operational Manager's assignment was recorded in the database and visible on their own dashboard. Additionally, the functionality to actually accept these new assignments had been commented out in the `ClientDetailsView`.\n\n### What I fixed:\n1. **Removed Overzealous Filter**: I removed the `isAccepted` condition from `AssignedClient.tsx` in all the affected media subdirectories (`multi-role/pages/photographer`, `videographer`, `drone`) as well as the generic `media/pages/AssignedClient.tsx`. This ensures that freshly assigned tasks flow into the employee's pending list immediately.\n<truncated 617 bytes>"}
